      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Certainly! Here's your polished review:\n\n---\n\nI recently dined at 'L'Essence' in Lyon, and the experience was appreciable. The atmosphere exuded an upscale ambiance through its dim lighting and quiet environment. Although the atmosphere was refined, it felt somewhat stiff. The culinary excellence of the duck confit was mesmerizing, with its tender meat and crispy skin. The accompanying sauce was equally rich and delectable. As for dessert, the lemon tart failed to impress due to its overly sour taste.\n\nThe service was noted to be swift, though it appeared a bit rushed, detracting slightly from the overall experience. While 'L'Essence' does deliver quality cuisine, guests might find it best appreciated in the more relaxed company.\n\n---\n\nUsing fewer adjectives allowed the review to maintain an authentic tone while still delivering a clear and helpful overview of your dining encounter. This approach likely produced a better richness score while keeping the review engaging and professional.",
